+* `use_parts`: after 404/403/409 (assignee, `in_progress`), any item whose `part` is an existing
+  part at the order's asset's site and whose `quantity` is an integer >= 1 but more than the part's
+  stock makes the whole call a 409, even if other items (or extra keys) are invalid. A part at
+  another site is not a valid part, so asking too much of it is a 400. Field errors are reported
+  as `items[i].part` / `items[i].quantity`. Cancelling keeps usages and stock as they are.
+* `POST /api/part_usages` is 403; `PATCH`/`DELETE /api/part_usages/{id}` are 404 for an unknown
+  id, otherwise 403. Changing parts through PATCH never emits `low_stock`.
